invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_blocks_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_mont_mul runs the blocks for every even word count, not
  only a multiple of 4, so a count of 6, 10 or more reads a last block of
  four words past the operands and past the running sum, and writes
  words that are no product. bin/rsa_blocks_equiv_test compares the
  multiplication with rsa_mont64.c's loops at every word count from 1 to
  64.

--- old
    if (k % 4 == 0) {
        mont_mul_blocks(o, a, b, mod);
--- new
    if (k % 2 == 0) {
        mont_mul_blocks(o, a, b, mod);
